WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
I went to the bank the other day,

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.450
socially safe, of course, wearing my mask,

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.330
and the tellers told me,

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.540
and this is something that's interesting

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.040
'cause it's sort of a
nationwide phenomenon.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.230
They told me they had run out of coins.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.700
Did you know this was going on?

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.670
Apparently we're going
through a coin shortage.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.100
Yeah, you see it in lots
of different stores.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.890
They say no change. I guess
it's like a COVID thing.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.140
Yeah, well anyway, the
US Mint is scrambling

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.085
to figure out just what to do

00:00:27.085 --> 00:00:29.840
and they just released this ad.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.050
Take a look.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.789
Hi, I'm Diana Fowler,
Director of the US Mint.

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:37.500
As an unforeseen side effect
of COVID-19, for some reason,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.867
America is also now experiencing
a shortage of coins.

00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:42.720
(laughs) We don't know why either.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.272
So we're introducing a
replacement for coins.

00:00:46.272 --> 00:00:47.360
Coibs.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.480
Coibs are just like coins,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.216
except they're actually small rocks.

00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:53.251
[Man] Ah!

00:00:53.251 --> 00:00:54.310
It's a rock! (laughing)

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.960
Coibs are about the same size as coins

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.240
and they come from the ground,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.760
which means we're less
likely to run out of them.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.290
And from now on all
businesses have to take them

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.393
as legal tender.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.793
Coibs.

00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:08.160
It's a new thing we're trying
because we ran out of coins.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.910
Sorry, can you cut?

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.093
I'm Glenn, a writer at Conan.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.373
Does this sketch idea like
even make sense at all?

00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:20.762
Oh

00:01:23.421 --> 00:01:24.254
Yeah.

00:01:24.254 --> 00:01:25.087
Yes.

00:01:25.087 --> 00:01:26.450
Yeah.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.970
Yeah, yeah, it's great.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:30.240
Yeah, I've just been
spending a lot of time inside

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.720
by myself with like no one else around.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.790
And since my brain just went, like,

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:37.653
what if, what if coins were rocks?

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:43.540
Well, and like read the
news at all right now,

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.210
like it's hard to be
creative and make stuff.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.350
Oh, absolutely. I totally get it.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.183
Totally, yes.

00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.016
Of course.

00:01:51.016 --> 00:01:52.570
Oh my God I totally, like me,

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.720
I'm trying to finish this novel.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.820
So my creative brain is not a little bit

00:01:56.918 --> 00:02:00.890
not doing good stuff 'cause
I'm just so isolated right now

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.680
that I think I'm going crazy.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.787
No, no, no, absolutely not.

00:02:04.787 --> 00:02:07.160
Not losing your mind. I swear.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.860
The concept of the
sketch is a little weird.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.900
It's kind of it's a little, I mean, yeah.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.470
Yeah.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:20.083
What is it funner if coins were bugs

00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:22.508
(laughing) that a good idea

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.800
Oh, that's funny.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.633
That's good

00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:25.466
That's very fresh

00:02:25.466 --> 00:02:26.830
That makes sense. Okay.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.530
That's oh yeah

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.363
Thank you.

